  "details": "Add an optional Live Photo-style feature to the VRChat camera that saves a few seconds before and after a photo is taken.\n\nA possible implementation could work similarly to ShadowPlay, where VRChat continuously keeps a short rolling frame buffer in memory. Pressing the shutter would save the buffered few seconds leading up to the photo, along with a few seconds afterward, while still saving the normal full-quality image.\n\nThis would be great for capturing spontaneous moments, reactions, avatar animations, or anything that happens immediately before or after pressing the shutter without needing to constantly record full video sessions.\n\nIdeally, the buffer length could be configurable or simply kept to a short default such as 2–3 seconds before and after the photo.",
